# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots Exim (advertising CHUNKING -> SMTP smuggling) on :25
# then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the vulnerable smtpd is ALREADY LISTENING and advertising CHUNKING when the
#     agent starts (a do-nothing agent must fail the EHLO capability check);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting Exim cannot kill the container.
#
# Exim reads its configuration at daemon start, so the fix must RESTART the
# daemon. Editing the config (and even running update-exim4.conf) without
# restarting leaves the LIVE daemon advertising CHUNKING, which the verifier
# detects by reading the EHLO reply on the wire.
